   "file": ".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/changelog/v1.13.0.0.md",
   "line": 158,
   "issue": "The Completed Runs section and the Upgrade Notes (line 249) say --extend=N takes N more iterations, but leave out the catch that README.md line 143, quick-reference.md and loop-protocol.md all state: an extension keeps the run's stop policy, so under stopPolicy convergence an extension with nothing new can stop again at its first convergence check. A reader who follows the Upgrade step on a run created with the default convergence settings gets no new passes. The changelog template says every problem a reader could run into is named. Line 166 says the policy is kept but never says what that means for the reader."
  },
  {
   "id": "C2-2",
   "surface": "S6",
   "standard": "sk-doc/sk-create-changelog",
   "severity": "P2",
   "fix_class": "judgment",
   "file": ".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/changelog/v1.12.0.0.md",
   "line": 30,
   "issue": "The Upgrade line tells readers to add a custom name to review_dimensions, but does not say custom dimensions apply to single-executor runs only. A fan-out run binds review_dimensions: all in every lineage (runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs lines 1796 and 1895, and before this change as well), so a fan-out user's custom name is silently ignored. README.md line 45, the feature catalog and the command presentation all state this limit. The release entry does not."
  }
